1
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:14,560
So today we have a question for listeners, and it is: what’s your favourite room, and why?

2
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,940
Our first caller is … hello.

3
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,120
What’s your name?

4
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,760
Hi there! My name’s Jo.

5
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:26,500
OK Jo, so tell us, what’s your favourite room?

6
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:29,582
It’s my grandfather’s playroom.

7
00:00:29,582 --> 00:00:33,600
Your grandfather’s got a playroom? Really?

8
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:34,620
Yeah.

9
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,480
It’s the room with his model trains.

10
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:42,180
My grandad still lives in the house he lived in when he was a boy.

11
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,940
And he has a little room with his trains.

12
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:48,760
I love looking at his trains.

13
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,081
OK. And why is it special for you?

14
00:00:53,081 --> 00:01:00,040
Because he’s so happy there, and we sit and talk, and I feel very relaxed.

15
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,160
It’s lovely.

16
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:03,580
It sounds great, Jo.

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:04,772
Thank you.

18
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:10,147
Now who’s next? What’s your name and what’s your favourite room?

19
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:11,041
Hi.

20
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:16,138
I’m Andrew and my favourite room is the music room at my school.

21
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:19,250
OK, Andrew. And why’s that?

22
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:28,503
It’s because I love playing the drums, but I can’t have drums at home, so I go into the music room at school and practise there.

23
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:29,920
After school.

24
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:31,100
No one cares.

25
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,193
I have a lot of fun!

26
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:36,862
Sounds good to me! Thanks, Andrew.

27
00:01:36,862 --> 00:01:39,900
Next caller please! Hello!

28
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,700
Hello, I’m Paula.

29
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:47,120
My favourite room is our kitchen at home.

30
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:54,500
I love it there because that’s where all of us sit and have our breakfast and dinner, and we’re a family together.

31
00:01:55,110 --> 00:01:58,480
It makes me feel really nice and warm.

32
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:02,820
Nice and warm. That’s a good reason.

33
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:06,980
Yeah, and kind of … I don’t know, safe.

34
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:09,962
Excellent, Paula, thank you.

35
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:12,340
And now we have … hello?

36
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,820
Hi. Tom here.

37
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:22,060
I don’t know if it’s really my favourite room, but the best room in my whole life was in a hotel.

38
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:26,220
Oh right. That’s interesting! Tell us more!

39
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:37,060
We all went to Brazil last year, and we got to the hotel in Rio de Janeiro very early in the morning and it was still quite dark.

40
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:43,380
But then the day started and I opened the window to see Copacabana beach.

41
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:44,320
Brilliant!

42
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:46,220
I loved that room.

43
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:48,646
We were there for five days and …

44
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:51,153
Thanks, Tom. I’m sorry, there’s no more time.

45
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:51,680
OK, now let’s … .
